  "kind": "statement",
  "title": "Standard affine opens of Proj",
  "statement": "Each positive-degree homogeneous $f$ determines an open subscheme\n$D_+(f)\\subseteq\\operatorname{Proj}(R)$ and a canonical isomorphism\n\n$$\nD_+(f)\\cong\\operatorname{Spec}(R_{(f),0}).\n$$\n\nIf homogeneous elements $(f_i)$ generate $R_+$, the $D_+(f_i)$ cover\n$\\operatorname{Proj}(R)$.",
  "source": {
    "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-nagata-compactification/sk-def-nagata-sketch-data/prop-nagata-proj-standard-open.md",
    "place": "node prop-nagata-proj-standard-open, order 11"
  },
  "stmt_deps": [
    "def-nagata-affine-proj",
    "def-nagata-homogeneous-localization-degree-zero"
  ],
  "proof": [
    {
      "text": "The standard-open isomorphism is `Proj.basicOpenIsoSpec`.\nThe cover assertion is\n`AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.iSup_basicOpen_eq_top`; its hypothesis\nthat the chosen homogeneous family generates the irrelevant ideal is the\nassumption in the statement.\nThus no independently glued affine scheme is being used.",
      "uses": [],
      "elementary": null
    }
  ],
